[
 {
  "cmd": "get out of cot",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 51,
  "parentBeforeName": "army cot",
  "parentAfter": 71,
  "parentAfterName": "Your Tent",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "You push yourself up and manage to get out of the cot. Your legs are a little wobbly, though, and your head swims.\n \nYou hear a plane flying high overhead, outside the tent.\n \n>"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "s",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 71,
  "parentBeforeName": "Your Tent",
  "parentAfter": 72,
  "parentAfterName": "Outside Your Tent",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "Outside Your Tent\nYou are on an east/west path on the north side of the encampment. To the south you can see a firepit and to the north is the entrance to your tent. Everything is oddly quiet, unsettling, creating a feeling of floating anxiety. The stillness seems to enhance the eerie quality of the desert, the feeling of being truly alone. There's a small hole in the sand, a remnant of your excavation attempts.\n \nYou crane your neck and see a plane, high overhead, circling the encampment.\n \n>"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "sw",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 72,
  "parentBeforeName": "Outside Your Tent",
  "parentAfter": 68,
  "parentAfterName": "Outside Supply Tent",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "Outside Supply Tent\nYou're on a north/south path on the west edge of the encampment. Directly to the west is the supply tent, its flaps open, still in the hot, quiet air. To the east you can see the central firepit, a reminder of your being alone. A row of thickets, impossible to make any progress through even with a machete, grows along the western edge of the camp directly to the north and south of the tent. There's a small hole in the sand, a remnant of your excavation attempts.\n \nYou crane your neck and see a plane, high overhead, circling the encampment.\n \n>"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "w",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 68,
  "parentBeforeName": "Outside Supply Tent",
  "parentAfter": 69,
  "parentAfterName": "Supply Tent",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "Supply Tent\nYou are in a tent, very much like your own -- a tent which had originally contained the supplies for your expedition. You notice, however, that most of the items which were here just yesterday have vanished with your workers. The tent looks as if it's been cleaned out and, as your stomach growls, the empty tent ironically reminds you of a turkey carcass picked clean after a huge Thanksgiving meal. Through the open tent flaps to the east you can see the firepit. If only one of the workers had remained behind, you would make him pay.\nStuck in the sand, handle down, is a small pick axe.\nHalf buried in the sand, in the corner of the tent, is a shovel.\n \nIt sounds as if the plane is c"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "get pickaxe",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 69,
  "parentBeforeName": "Supply Tent",
  "parentAfter": 69,
  "parentAfterName": "Supply Tent",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "Taken.\n \nIt sounds as if the plane is circling.\n \n>"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "get shovel",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 69,
  "parentBeforeName": "Supply Tent",
  "parentAfter": 69,
  "parentAfterName": "Supply Tent",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "Taken.\n \nIt sounds as if the plane is flying off.\n \n>"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "e",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 69,
  "parentBeforeName": "Supply Tent",
  "parentAfter": 68,
  "parentAfterName": "Outside Supply Tent",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "Outside Supply Tent\n \nA small speck descending from the plane overhead gets larger until you see a crate, dangling from a parachute.\n \n>"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "se",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 68,
  "parentBeforeName": "Outside Supply Tent",
  "parentAfter": 64,
  "parentAfterName": "Outside Work Tent",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "Outside Work Tent\nYou are on an east/west path, directly to the north of the work tent. To the north you can see the firepit and, beyond that, your tent. The work tent borders an endless vista of fine, burning sand stretching out to the south. There's an enlarged hole in the sand, a remnant of your excavation attempts.\n \nAt last, your luck seems to be changing. A large crate lands right before you, its parachute flapping in the breeze. The parachute breaks away from the crate and drifts off in the wind.\n \n>"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "s",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 64,
  "parentBeforeName": "Outside Work Tent",
  "parentAfter": 62,
  "parentAfterName": "Work Tent",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "Work Tent\nYou are in a tent which used to house the workers and their personal effects. Looking around, taking in the stripped and bare surroundings, you feel surprised that they even left the canvas walls. You quickly realize that they took what they needed -- taking everything would have been more trouble than it was worth. From the looks of things they cleared out quickly but quietly.\nTacked up to the inside of one of the tent flaps is a note.\nSitting in the sand, bulging a little, is a beaten-up knapsack.\n \n>"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "read note",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 62,
  "parentBeforeName": "Work Tent",
  "parentAfter": 62,
  "parentAfterName": "Work Tent",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "The note reads:\n \nFi aman Allah! \nHereafter you shall pursue your fool dream of the hidden pyramid and its riches alone. May the jackals feed well on your bones. We have left you what you need to get back, though we hope you do not. We put several things you treasure above life itself inside your trunk, locked with your precious padlock, but we could not bear to part with the key. Especially after what you said of our rites. We hope the drug we placed in your drink did you harm. If not, we are at least satisfied you slept especially soundly while we cleaned out the camp.\n \nFarewell\n \n>"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "get knapsack",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 62,
  "parentBeforeName": "Work Tent",
  "parentAfter": 62,
  "parentAfterName": "Work Tent",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "(wearing it)\nYou swing the knapsack over your shoulders and it settles on your back as its cover flap closes.\n \n>"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "n",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 62,
  "parentBeforeName": "Work Tent",
  "parentAfter": 64,
  "parentAfterName": "Outside Work Tent",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "Outside Work Tent\nLying in the sand is a wooden packing crate.\n \n>"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "n",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 64,
  "parentBeforeName": "Outside Work Tent",
  "parentAfter": 78,
  "parentAfterName": "Fire Pit",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "Fire Pit\nYou are in the center of the encampment, standing before a charred pit, a hole dug in the sand surrounded by blackened rocks. The night breezes have already started the reclamation work of the desert, covering most of the pit's bottom. You can see your tent to the north, the work tent to the south, and the supply tent to the west. Far off to the east, through the heat waves rising off the shifting sands, you can see gentle, rolling dunes. There's a small hole in the sand, a remnant of your excavation attempts.\nHalf covered with sand is a bright piece of foil which catches your eye.\nSitting by a rock is what looks like a matchbook.\n \n>"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "get matchbook",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 78,
  "parentBeforeName": "Fire Pit",
  "parentAfter": 78,
  "parentAfterName": "Fire Pit",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "Taken.\n \n>"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "n",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 78,
  "parentBeforeName": "Fire Pit",
  "parentAfter": 72,
  "parentAfterName": "Outside Your Tent",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "Outside Your Tent\n \n>"
 },
 {
  "cmd": "n",
  "tag": null,
  "parentBefore": 72,
  "parentBeforeName": "Outside Your Tent",
  "parentAfter": 71,
  "parentAfterName": "Your Tent",
  "playerId": 223,
  "reply": "Your Tent\nThere is an army cot here.\nAt the foot of the cot is a large, unwieldy trunk. The trunk is closed and locked with a padlock.\n \n>"
 },
 {
